					"severity": "P3",
					"title": "Missing 'Not for' exclusion for authoring-agent-skills, contradicting the new convention",
					"text": "🟢 **P3**\n\n**Missing 'Not for' exclusion for authoring-agent-skills, contradicting the new convention**\n\n`description-conventions.md` rule 4 says exclusions must be added in both directions. `authoring-agent-skills` now excludes `agent-instructions`, and `best-practices-for-agentic-development` does too. This description still claims \"a SKILL.md\" and \"edit this skill\" with no exclusion pointing back. The two skills' triggers overlap, which is the ambiguity this PR sets out to remove. Add a short `Not for creating skills in the agent-skills repo (authoring-agent-skills)` clause.\n\n<!-- ai-review:fp=style|skills/agent-instructions/SKILL.md|2aaa014bc70e8ade.0 -->"
				},
				{
