					"path": "scripts/lint-descriptions.py",
					"line": 49,
					"severity": "P3",
					"title": "Length is measured after whitespace normalization, not on the parsed description",
					"text": "🟢 **P3**\n\n**Length is measured after whitespace normalization, not on the parsed description**\n\n`\" \".join(description.split())` collapses runs of whitespace and newlines before the length checks. A quoted or literal-block description with repeated spaces or blank lines can pass the 400/1000 thresholds here while still using more characters in the real listing, which cuts at 1,536. Keep the parsed string for counting. If you want normalization for the prefix check, apply it only there.\n\n<!-- ai-review:fp=bug|scripts/lint-descriptions.py|78f201a565bb6740.0 -->"
