					"path": "skills/developing-claude-code-plugins/scripts/parse-frontmatter.sh",
					"line": 54,
					"severity": "P2",
					"title": "Quote-truncation regex breaks values containing escaped or doubled quotes",
					"text": "🟡 **P2**\n\n**Quote-truncation regex breaks values containing escaped or doubled quotes**\n\nThe new `match(out, /^\"[^\"]*\"/)` keeps only the text up to the first closing quote, and the next line then strips the outer quotes. A double-quoted value with escaped quotes, such as `description: \"Use when \\\"x\\\" happens\"`, matches `\"Use when \\\"`. The result is the truncated `Use when \\`. A single-quoted value with a doubled quote, such as `'it''s'`, is cut to `it`. Before this change the full text was returned. The validators then check a truncated value, so they can give wrong pass/fail results for descriptions or names that contain quotes. Match the closing quote while honoring `\\\"` in double-quoted values and `''` in single-quoted values, or only strip a trailing comment after a properly closed quoted string. Add a fixture for an escaped-quote value.\n\n<!-- ai-review:fp=bug|skills/developing-claude-code-plugins/scripts/parse-frontmatter.sh|7a0fa51f1f4fa108.0 -->"
				},
